{"name":"Elegant Earth","hex":"#ac8e73","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elegant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characterised by or exhibiting elegance; having grace, refinement, or tasteful simplicity.","Characterised by minimalism and intuitiveness while preserving exactness and precision."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elegant parrot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elegant"},{"term":"earth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Earth (“the third planet of the Solar System, upon which humans live”)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Soil.","Any general rock-based material."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elegance","blocks":[{"text":"Elegance is beauty that shows unusual effectiveness and simplicity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Pythagorean_proof_%281%29.svg/330px-Pythagorean_proof_%281%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elegance"},{"title":"Earth","blocks":[{"text":"Earth is the third planet from the Sun and the only astronomical object known to harbor life. This is made possible by Earth being an ocean world, the only one in the Solar System sustaining liquid surface water. Almost all of Earth's water is contained in its ocean, which covers 70.8% of Earth's crust. The remaining 29.2% of Earth's crust is dry land, which is predominantly located within Earth's land hemisphere in the form of continental landmasses. Most of Earth's land is at least somewhat humid and covered by vegetation, while large ice sheets at Earth's polar deserts retain more water than Earth's groundwater, lakes, rivers, and atmospheric water combined. Earth's crust consists of slowly moving tectonic plates, which interact to produce mountain ranges, volcanoes, and earthquakes. Earth has a liquid outer core that generates a magnetosphere capable of deflecting most of the destructive solar winds and cosmic radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Meteosat-12-fci-march-equinox-2025-noon.jpg/330px-Meteosat-12-fci-march-equinox-2025-noon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Soulacroix_-_Elegance_Of_The_Epoque.jpg/500px-Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Soulacroix_-_Elegance_Of_The_Epoque.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Soulacroix_-_Elegance_Of_The_Epoque.jpg/500px-Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Soulacroix_-_Elegance_Of_The_Epoque.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Elegance of the Epoque by Frédéric Soulacroix","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Soulacroix_-_Elegance_Of_The_Epoque.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/The_Mysterious_Case_of_the_Disappearing_Dust.jpg/500px-The_Mysterious_Case_of_the_Disappearing_Dust.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/The_Mysterious_Case_of_the_Disappearing_Dust.jpg/1280px-The_Mysterious_Case_of_the_Disappearing_Dust.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/The_Mysterious_Case_of_the_Disappearing_Dust.jpg/500px-The_Mysterious_Case_of_the_Disappearing_Dust.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A depiction of the early Solar System's protoplanetary disk from which Earth and other Solar System bodies were formed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Mysterious_Case_of_th